        "original_id": "402eb7d0-d3d9-5174-ab4a-e1cc78950f45",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tess Asplund, David Lagerlof\n- Organizations: Nordic Resistance Movement\n- Concepts: viral image, Neo-Nazi movement\n- Places: Sweden, Finland, Norway\n\nFacts:\n- David Lagerlof is the photographer of a viral image showing Tess Asplund facing uniformed members of the Nordic Resistance Movement with her fist raised.\n- The Nordic Resistance Movement is a Nordic Neo-Nazi movement.\n- The Nordic Resistance Movement exists in Sweden, Finland, and Norway.\n- The Nordic Resistance Movement is known in Swedish as \"Nordiska Motståndsrörelsen\" with the abbreviation NMR.\n- The Nordic Resistance Movement is known in Norwegian as \"Nordiske motstandsbevegelsen\" with the abbreviation NMB.\n- The Nordic Resistance Movement is known in Finnish as \"Pohjoismainen vastarintaliike\" with the abbreviation PVL.\n- The Nordic Resistance Movement is known in Danish as \"Nordiske modstandsbevægelse\" with the abbreviation NMB.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
